A mere 26 days after my first ascension ever, I managed to pull off my
second!

After playing a rogue, I started trying for a caveman win, so I set up
the config file for a caveman of a random species each time.  I ended
up with a dwarf for my winning run.

My little dog named Slasher, surprisingly, never died.  He did,
however, get polymorphed into a quivering blob via a trap deep within
the mines.  Using a wand of polymorph, I altered him several times
until he finally became a clay golem.  Unfortunately, he was still
very, very slow, and without a magic whistle I had little choice but
to leave him.  Fortuantely, he stayed there and kept my stash safe,
and was always eager to greet me when I returned.

Anu granted me Snickersnee, so I was able to use longswords with some
reasonable amount of skill; I subsequently received Fire Brand and
Demonbane.  I figured the skill would be nice if I wanted Excalibur
later on, but in the meantime I worked on looking for a mace to
prepare for the Sceptre.

The fight with the Chromatic Dragon was harrowing.  I had acquired an
amulet of life saving shortly before the encounter.  The Dragon
climbed all of the stairs through the quest levels, all the way back
up to my ancestral caves, with an Arch-Lich in tow, tormenting me the
whole way.  I killed them both on the top level and retrieved the
Sceptre of Might (and genocided liches shortly after, good gravy!).

Since Sokoban yielded a Bag of Holding, and since Cavemen can't
#twoweapon, I took the shield of relection off of the statue of
Perseus after slaying Medusa, who I subsequently tinned for posterity.

I began seeing Nazgul as I headed downward, and was hoping to complete
a set of rings; I only managed to find six.

Before I reached the Castle, I was fortunate enough to be crowned the
Hand of Elbereth.  I decided then and there that I must succeed!

I figured out the Castle tune in record time and headed in, and after
stocking up on the essentials and sitting on the throne, I headed for
the Valley of the Dead, where Yeenoghu greeted me with a platter of
cocktail weenies and a whip.

Cruising through the demon princes (I killed Juiblex in like two hits,
what's up with that?), I located Vlad's Tower, ran to the top and
pushed him over, jacked his Candelabrum and his water-walking boots,
and said good-day.  Shortly after, I found an egg which hatched into a
chickatrice, which promptly stepped on a polymorph trap and turned
into an orange dragon.  Finally, an SUV that suits my needs!

The dragon lasted me through defeating the Wizard (also tinned for
prosperity) and all the way down to Moloch's Sanctum, where he was
promptly disintegrated into nothing by a black dragon.  My stay in the
Sanctum was punctuated by another encounter with the Wizard and one of
his clones.

I made a mad dash to the top, stopping at the stashes to get the rest
of my gold, gems and liquor for the ride up.  I also #dipped for
Excalibur and #named Sting and Orcrist, just to bolster my list of
artifacts.  I launched myself into the Elemental Planes, where I
learned that conflict is the greatest intrinsic ever, and that it also
makes the game painfully slow, as every monster visible on the screen
seems to have to attack another monster and step on a trap every turn.

I turned off conflict in order to receive a guardian angel upon
reaching the Astral Plane.  I managed to fight all of the riders his
time (I skipped Death on my previous go) and found the correct altar
on my third try (alas, my angel was slain just before entering the
room!).  I rushed in and locked the door immediately.

Pulling my wand of wishing from my everfull bag, I wished for an
icebox, which, thankfully, only spawned with one corpse in it, and it
was one I could lift!  I then wrested the wand's final charge for a
blessed succubus figurine, because that is what adventurers do.  I
loaded up the icebox with booze and tins of black pudding (delicious
relaxing snacks in the afterlife)and made sure I was set to ascend.  I
used a figurine of a skeleton I had wished for earlier, so that he
could be added to my point total.

I offered the Amulet to Anu, and as the thunder rolled, I shouted,
"Wait!  WAIT!  I left my icebox on the altar!"  Arrrrgh!  At least the
figurine wasn't in it.

I don't have the character dump patch, so I took screenshots and
clipped them together.  Here's the important stuff:
http://img505.imageshack.us/img505/8683/nhjoccavemanascend03140pp4.png

Now I may relax in the hereafter, though once again I may have to
barter for a cold drink.  If anyone is headed to the high altar of
Anu, would you please send up my icebox?!


